IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era-types`
IMPORT `era-periods`
IMPORT `era-notice`

-- Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK) — GOAL 3: REDUNDANCY PAYMENT.
--
--   "Is the employee entitled to a redundancy payment, and how much?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1996-18.txt — ss 135, 136, 139,
-- 140, 141, 145, 155, 162, 163(2), 164, 207B, 227.

§ `Goal 3 — redundancy payment`

-- s 136(1): dismissed "if (and only if)— (a) the contract ... is terminated
-- by the employer (whether with or without notice), (b) he is employed under
-- a limited term contract and that contract terminates by virtue of the
-- limiting event without being renewed under the same contract, or (c) the
-- employee terminates the contract ... in circumstances in which he is
-- entitled to terminate it without notice by reason of the employer's
-- conduct."
@ref s 136(1)
GIVEN t IS A `Termination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is dismissed under s 136(1) by` t IF
    CONSIDER t's `how it ended`
    WHEN `terminated by the employee otherwise` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 163(2) "an employee who has been dismissed by his employer shall, unless
-- the contrary is proved, be presumed to have been so dismissed by reason of
-- redundancy." Not proved either way (NOTHING): presumed.
@ref ss 139(1), 163(2)
GIVEN r IS A `Redundancy facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dismissal is taken to be by reason of redundancy under` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `dismissed by reason of redundancy`
    WHEN JUST b  THEN b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- s 155 "An employee does not have any right to a redundancy payment unless
-- he has been continuously employed for a period of not less than two years
-- ending with the relevant date." (relevant date as extended by s 145(5))
@ref s 155
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`, t IS A `Termination`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the qualifying period in s 155 is met by` emp `for` t IF
    emp `has been continuously employed for` 24 `months ending with` (`the relevant date for ss 155 and 162(1) of` emp `and` t)

§§ `Claims (s 164)`

-- s 164(1) "An employee does not have any right to a redundancy payment
-- unless, before the end of the period of six months beginning with the
-- relevant date— (a) the payment has been agreed and paid, (b) the employee
-- has made a claim for the payment by notice in writing given to the
-- employer, (c) a question as to the employee's right to, or the amount of,
-- the payment has been referred to an employment tribunal, or (d) a
-- complaint relating to his dismissal has been presented by the employee
-- under section 111." The relevant date is the one in s 145(2): s 145(5)
-- extends it only for ss 155, 162(1) and 227(3).
@ref s 164(1)
@export The last day of the six months beginning with the relevant date under s 164(1) of the Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK), before whose end a redundancy payment must be agreed and paid, claimed in writing, referred to a tribunal or a s 111 complaint presented (a tribunal reference is extended for early conciliation by s 207B). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Termination`  @desc The day the contract ended (the relevant date in s 145(2))
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the s 164(1) period for` t MEANS
    `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` (`the relevant date under s 145(2) of` t)

-- s 164(5): s 207B applies for the purposes of (1)(c) and (2).
@ref s 164(1), (5)
GIVEN t IS A `Termination`, r IS A `Redundancy facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a step in s 164(1) was taken in time for` t `with` r IF
        `a step on` (r's `agreed and paid on`) `came on or before` limit
    OR  `a step on` (r's `written claim given on`) `came on or before` limit
    OR  `a step on` (r's `referred to a tribunal on`) `came on or before` (`the time limit` limit `of the period beginning with` (`the relevant date under s 145(2) of` t) `extended under s 207B by` (r's `early conciliation`))
    OR  `a step on` (r's `unfair dismissal complaint presented on`) `came on or before` limit
    WHERE
        limit MEANS `the last day of the s 164(1) period for` t

-- s 164(2) "An employee is not deprived of his right to a redundancy payment
-- by subsection (1) if, during the period of six months immediately
-- following the period mentioned in that subsection, the employee— (a) makes
-- a claim for the payment by notice in writing given to the employer, (b)
-- refers to an employment tribunal a question as to his right to, or the
-- amount of, the payment, or (c) presents a complaint relating to his
-- dismissal under section 111, and it appears to the tribunal to be just and
-- equitable that the employee should receive a redundancy payment." s 164(5):
-- s 207B applies for the purposes of (2).
@ref s 164(2), (5)
GIVEN t IS A `Termination`, r IS A `Redundancy facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a step in s 164(2) was taken in the next six months for` t `with` r IF
        r's `tribunal finds a late claim just and equitable`
    AND (   `a step on` (r's `written claim given on`) `came on or before` limit
         OR `a step on` (r's `referred to a tribunal on`) `came on or before` limit
         OR `a step on` (r's `unfair dismissal complaint presented on`) `came on or before` limit)
    WHERE
        limit MEANS `the time limit` unextended `of the period beginning with` secondStart `extended under s 207B by` (r's `early conciliation`)
        unextended MEANS `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` secondStart
        secondStart MEANS `the day` 1 `days after` (`the last day of the s 164(1) period for` t)

§§ `Entitlement and amount (ss 135, 140, 141, 162)`

-- s 135(1) "An employer shall pay a redundancy payment to any employee of
-- his if the employee— (a) is dismissed by the employer by reason of
-- redundancy", subject to ss 140-144, 155-161 and 164 (s 135(2)).
@ref ss 135, 136, 140, 141, 155, 163(2), 164
@export Whether an employee is entitled to a redundancy payment under s 135(1)(a) of the Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK): dismissed (s 136(1)) by reason of redundancy (presumed under s 163(2) unless the contrary is proved), not excluded by s 140 (summary dismissal for conduct), s 141 (unreasonable refusal of suitable employment) or another exclusion, continuously employed for two years ending with the relevant date (s 155), and a step taken in time under s 164. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`        @desc The day continuous employment began
      t   IS A `Termination`      @desc How and when the contract ended
      r   IS A `Redundancy facts` @desc The reason, the exclusions, and the dates of any payment, claim, reference or complaint
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to a redundancy payment` emp `for` t `with` r IF
        `the employee is dismissed under s 136(1) by` t
    AND `the dismissal is taken to be by reason of redundancy under` r
    AND NOT (r's `dismissed for conduct within s 140(1)`)
    AND NOT (r's `unreasonably refused suitable employment`)
    AND NOT (r's `excluded otherwise`)
    AND `the qualifying period in s 155 is met by` emp `for` t
    AND (   `a step in s 164(1) was taken in time for` t `with` r
         OR `a step in s 164(2) was taken in the next six months for` t `with` r)

-- s 162(1)-(3), with a week's pay capped by s 227(1)(c), over the period
-- ending with the relevant date (extended by s 145(5)).
@ref ss 162(1)-(3), 227(1)(c)
@export The amount of a redundancy payment under s 162 of the Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK): for each year of continuous employment (up to twenty, counted back from the relevant date as extended by s 145(5)) one and a half weeks' pay in a year the employee was 41 or over, one week's pay in a year they were 22 or over, otherwise half a week's pay, with a week's pay capped at £751 by s 227(1). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN emp IS AN `Employee`    @desc Date of birth, the day continuous employment began, and a week's pay
      t   IS A `Termination`  @desc How and when the contract ended
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of a redundancy payment under s 162 for` emp `and` t MEANS
        `the weeks' pay for the years of employment of` emp `ending with` (`the relevant date for ss 155 and 162(1) of` emp `and` t)
    TIMES `a week's pay, capped under s 227(1), for` emp
